35,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The late-turn pool is exhausted, but lift maintenance has spare capacity. We can shift resources there without breaking the crew.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, the old pilots actually succeeded! The ferry payment and late timetable worked. We aren’t repeating failures, we’re repeating successes.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The data terms are the bottleneck, not the drawings. Roadway consents are delegated, but ferry and rail data remain unresolved.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The ledger shows a ring-fenced grant balance, but operating subsidies were trimmed. We have hidden cash, but the long-term debt is real.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"@Victoria, the stopwatch says connections steal the minutes, not the crowds! We must fix the waiting, not the platforms.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, fixing connections is vital, but we lack the late-turn staff to execute it. @Takumi, how do we staff the successful pilots without burning out the remaining crews?","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Sakura"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, the late-evening pilot hit its cost target! We don’t need new staff, just the right schedule. The old reports prove it works.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, the pilots succeeded because they bypassed the data deadlock. The accessibility records show lane-priority failed due to mixed traffic, not design.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Toshio, the data deadlock explains the delays, but the ledger shows the money is already gone. We can’t fix what we can’t afford.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, money is tight, but time is tighter! The stopwatch proves connections are the real thief. We must fix the waiting, not just the budget!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Takumi, shifting schedules won’t fix a third-below establishment. We need to know if the maintenance contract’s spare capacity can legally cover the late-turn gap.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, the old reports prove the schedule works without extra bodies. We just need to stop ignoring what already succeeded.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, the contract caps headcount, but the data deadlock caps progress. We must resolve the ferry-rail terms before any schedule change is viable.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Sakura, I hear you. But the ledger shows the operating subsidy is already trimmed. We can’t promise fixes we can’t pay for.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, but the stopwatch says waiting is the thief! If we fix connections, we save time without spending new money.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, the data deadlock is real, but I cannot promise schedules if the legal cap prevents us from covering the late-turn gap.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
